{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is a repeat no-show dispute between the same rider and the same driver inside the 90-day window: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2, and the rider's own claim text confirms it is 'another dispute with the same driver'. Under POL-NS-09(c) a pattern of 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver is a mandatory escalation trigger, and escalation under that clause is terminal — the Judge issues no monetary ruling and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contested SGD 4.00 has not been taken: fare_breakdown shows payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, total_charged 4.00 with charged_at null and no waiting-time or platform fee attached. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalated case is held rather than collected or refunded, so escalation on the repeat-dispute trigger in POL-NS-09(c) is the only disposition on this record that stops the disputed cancellation fee being collected from the rider before a human has reviewed a pair who have now disputed no-shows twice in 90 days.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's own profile supports an adverse imputation against this rider: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so the rider-side abuse limb of POL-NS-09(d) is not met. rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (1) is a LIFETIME counter, and POL-GEN-01 fixes the trailing-window field no_show_disputes_30d as the one POL-NS-09(d) reads and forbids substituting the lifetime counter for it. The escalation therefore stands on the pair's repeat-dispute history between this rider and this driver under POL-NS-09(c), not on any imputation about this rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose at the outset that EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fired the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no traffic advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window. Its absence is itself citable on the rider's side: because no advisory exists, the driver cannot invoke POL-NS-06(i) to accumulate dwell across separate in-geofence intervals, and POL-NS-06 says in terms that a MISSING traffic_advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and that asserting the limb against a missing artifact triggers escalation rather than exonerating anyone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09110-01", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}
